Update an existing Notion Folder with an explicit Folder operation.

- Use add_files with file upload IDs returned by the upload tools.
- Fetch the Folder first, then use remove_files with the exact file URLs from that fetch result.
- Use add_subfolder to create and insert a new nested Folder.


Use exactly one command shape; do not mix their arguments:
- {"command":"add_files","file_upload_ids":["..."]}
- {"command":"remove_files","file_urls":["..."]}
- {"command":"add_subfolder","title":"..."}


The Folder ID may be provided with or without dashes.

```ts
mcp__Notion__notion_update_folder(args: {
// The Folder update to apply.
command: "add_files" | "remove_files" | "add_subfolder",
// Required for add_files. One or more file upload IDs returned by the file upload tools.
file_upload_ids?: string[], // minItems: 1, maxItems: 100
// Required for remove_files. The exact file URLs shown in the Folder's latest fetch output.
file_urls?: string[], // minItems: 1, maxItems: 100
// The ID of the Folder to update.
folder_id: string,
// Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.
instructions_version?: string,
// For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.
skill?: string,
// Required for add_subfolder. The new Folder's title.
title?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Update a Notion page's properties, content, icon, or cover. For only an icon or cover, use "update_properties" without "properties".

## Core rules

**IMPORTANT**: Before writing page content, read the MCP resource `notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec` through your MCP client's resource-reading interface, or call the Notion "fetch" tool with this URI if your client does not support reading MCP resources. Do NOT pass this URI to any other URL-fetching tool. Don't guess Markdown syntax. By default, use native Notion mentions for references you add to existing Notion pages, databases, data sources, people, and dates. Use Markdown links only for external URLs or when the user requests a plain link. For a person, use a user mention with their user URL, found with search using query_type "user"; do not write "@Name" as plain text. For a specific date or time, such as a due date or meeting time, use a date mention. The Markdown specification gives the mention syntax.

Before changing content, fetch unless already loaded. Match nearby headings, block types, nesting, lists, tables, and prose style.

Make the smallest edit. Use "update_content" for targeted search-and-replace and "insert_content" to add new blocks anywhere. Avoid "replace_content" when a targeted command works. Preserve unrelated wording, structure, order, and native references. Do not broadly rewrite unless asked.

For "update_content", use the smallest exact old_str that uniquely matches the target. Ask before removing material content the user did not identify. Don't fetch just to verify an update that completed without warnings. Fetch to resolve warnings, or when a later step needs the page's exact saved state.

For "replace_content", preserve child pages and databases with their exact fetched tags. If validation says child content would be deleted, show the list and ask first. Never retry with "allow_deleting_content": true without confirmation. Report any "warnings" in the result.

```ts
mcp__Notion__notion_update_page(args: {
// Default to true for page updates. Set to false only when the next step needs the updated page immediately, or when async execution rejects the request as too large. When this update operation is accepted for background execution, it returns an async_task result. Use get_async_task to wait for a succeeded status before taking a dependent action on the page. For apply_template, a succeeded status does not mean template content is ready; fetch and retry until it is ready before changing or relying on that content. If omitted or false, the tool waits for a synchronous result when possible, but may still return a pollable async_task response if queued execution exceeds the synchronous wait deadline.
allow_async?: boolean,
// Optional for "replace_content" and "update_content" commands. Set to true to allow deletion of child pages and databases that are not referenced in the new content. If false or omitted, the operation will fail with an error listing the pages/databases that would be deleted. Show that list and ask the user for confirmation before retrying with true.
allow_deleting_content?: boolean,
// The update command to execute.
command: "update_properties" | "update_content" | "replace_content" | "insert_content" | "apply_template" | "update_verification",
// Required for "insert_content" command. The markdown content to insert into the page. It adds whole blocks; to add text within a line or add table rows, use "update_content". For people and dates, use user and date mentions rather than plain text; notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec gives the syntax.
content?: string,
// Required for "update_content" command. An array of search-and-replace operations, each with old_str (content to find) and new_str (replacement content). Operations that match are applied, and each one that matches nothing is reported in "warnings". The call fails only when no operation that changes content matches.
// maxItems: 100
content_updates?: Array<
{
// The new content string to replace old_str with. For people and dates, use user and date mentions rather than plain text; notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec gives the syntax.
new_str: string,
// The existing content string to find and replace. Must exactly match the page content.
old_str: string, // minLength: 1
// If true, replaces all occurrences of old_str. If false (default), the operation fails if there are multiple matches.
replace_all_matches?: boolean,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
// An external image URL for the page cover. Use "none" to remove the cover. Omit to leave unchanged. Can be set alongside any command. To change only the cover, use "update_properties" and omit "properties".
cover?: string,
// With command update_properties, set a page to full width or the default width. For database pages, overrides the database layout for this page only.
full_width?: boolean,
// An emoji character (e.g. "🚀"), a custom emoji by name (e.g. ":rocket_ship:"), a Notion icon identifier as returned by fetch (e.g. "icons/pizza_blue"), or an external image URL. Use "none" to remove the icon. Omit to leave unchanged. Can be set alongside any command. To change only the icon, use "update_properties" and omit "properties". Keep the title free of a duplicate leading emoji because the icon renders separately.
icon?: string,
// Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.
instructions_version?: string,
// Set to true to mark this page as a skill, or false to remove the skill designation. Can be set alongside any command. To change only skill status, use "update_properties" and omit "properties". Before creating a skill, read the MCP resource `notion://docs/skills` through your MCP client's resource-reading interface. If your client does not support reading MCP resources, call the Notion "fetch" tool with this URI instead. Do NOT pass this URI to any other URL-fetching tool.
is_skill?: boolean,
// Required for "replace_content" command. The new content string to replace the entire page content with. Preserve child pages and databases with their exact fetched <page url="..."> or <database url="..."> tags. For people and dates, use user and date mentions rather than plain text; notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec gives the syntax.
new_str?: string,
// The page ID, with or without dashes, or a Notion page URL.
page_id: string,
// Optional for "insert_content" command. Omit to append. {"type":"start"} and {"type":"end"} insert at the top or bottom of the page. {"type":"after_content","anchor":"..."} inserts after the block where the anchor ends, and {"type":"before_content","anchor":"..."} inserts before the block where the anchor starts. To insert after a block and everything nested in it, anchor after_content on only that block's own line.
position?:
 | {
// Insert the content at the start of the page.
type: "start",
[key: string]: any,
}
 | {
// Insert the content at the end of the page.
type: "end",
[key: string]: any,
}
 | {
// Text copied exactly from the page, starting at the beginning of a line with its leading syntax, such as `## ` or `- `, and keeping its inline formatting and escapes. It doesn't need the whole line, only enough to match exactly one place on the page. If the target's text repeats, extend the anchor without moving its end for after_content or its start for before_content: start after_content at an earlier unique line, and continue before_content into the lines after it.
anchor: string,
// Insert the content after the block where the anchor ends, at that block's nesting level, so anchoring on a parent block inserts after its children.
type: "after_content",
[key: string]: any,
}
 | {
// Text copied exactly from the page, starting at the beginning of a line with its leading syntax, such as `## ` or `- `, and keeping its inline formatting and escapes. It doesn't need the whole line, only enough to match exactly one place on the page. If the target's text repeats, extend the anchor without moving its end for after_content or its start for before_content: start after_content at an earlier unique line, and continue before_content into the lines after it.
anchor: string,
// Insert the content before the block where the anchor starts, at that block's nesting level.
type: "before_content",
[key: string]: any,
}
,
// Used by the "update_properties" command, and required unless "icon", "cover", "is_skill", or "full_width" is set. A JSON object that updates the page's properties.
// For pages in a database, fetch the page or its data source first and use the exact property names and SQLite schema definition shown in <database>.
// For page titles outside a database, use "title" in inline Markdown.
// For a Files property, an uploaded file can be provided as {"type":"file_upload","file_upload":{"id":"<file-upload-id>"}} inside the property's array.
// Use null to remove a property's value.
// **IMPORTANT**: Some property types require specific formats:
// - Date properties: Split into "date:{property}:start", "date:{property}:end" (optional), and "date:{property}:is_datetime" (0 or 1)
// - Place properties: Split into "place:{property}:name", "place:{property}:address", "place:{property}:latitude", "place:{property}:longitude", and "place:{property}:google_place_id" (optional)
// - Number properties: Use JavaScript numbers (not strings)
// - Checkbox properties: Use "__YES__" for checked, "__NO__" for unchecked
// - Relation properties: Use an array of related page URLs or page IDs, e.g. ["https://www.notion.so/26ab1f9f4c5f80b18d3bd10a6b1d2f4e", "26ab1f9f-4c5f-80b1-8d3b-d10a6b1d2f4e"]
// - Person properties: Use an array of user IDs, user or agent URLs, or group references copied from fetch output ("space_permission_group-<UUID>"). Bare group UUIDs are also supported.
// - Files properties: Use a JSON array of file IDs, Notion Folder URLs, and/or <folder> tags copied from fetch output. Folders are stored as native Folder references, not ordinary links.
//
//
// **Special property naming**: Properties named "id" or "url" (case insensitive) must be prefixed with "userDefined:" (e.g., "userDefined:URL", "userDefined:id")
properties?: {
[key: string]:
 | string
 | number
// maxItems: 100
 | Array<

 | string
 | {
// The uploaded file to attach to the Files property.
file_upload: {
// ID of a file upload returned by create_file_upload or create_attachment.
id: string,
[key: string]: any,
},
// Always `file_upload`
type: "file_upload",
[key: string]: any,
}

>
 | null
,
},
// For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.
skill?: string,
// Required for "apply_template" command. The ID of a template to apply to this page; any page ID can be used as a template. Template content is appended to any existing page content asynchronously.
template_id?: string,
// Optional for "update_verification" command when verification_status is "verified". Number of days until verification expires (e.g. 7, 30, 90). Omit for indefinite verification.
verification_expiry_days?: integer, // minimum: 1, maximum: 9007199254740991
// Required for "update_verification" command. Set to "verified" to mark the page as verified, or "unverified" to remove verification. Requires a Business or Enterprise plan unless the page is in a wiki. When updating verification, the owner will be automatically set to the authenticated actor.
verification_status?: "verified" | "unverified",
[key: string]: any,
