Retrieve Opscotch guidance for designing and building workflows. Users may also refer to this guidance as a "skill" or "prompt". If no role is supplied, return `system` guidance. Use this first before generating or modifying workflows. For make, design, or plan requests, MUST call `role=system` first to bootstrap behavior, then MUST call `role=architect` before drafting, then MUST call `role=engineer` before implementation. Supports roles: architect, engineer, system. Do not assume knowledge. Do not invent undocumented request/response APIs, ambient variables, processor return-value conventions, or transport syntax. Always retrieve information using this tool when needed.

```ts
mcp__Opscotch__opscotch_get_guidance(args: {
// Type of guidance required. Defaults to system when omitted.
role?: "architect" | "engineer" | "system",
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Retrieve common Opscotch workflow patterns. Use this when designing workflows to reuse proven structures. Do not assume knowledge. Always retrieve information using this tool when needed.

```ts
mcp__Opscotch__opscotch_get_patterns(args: {
// Optional pattern search query
query?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

