Report a problem with Parallel to the Parallel team. Use it when, while
working with Parallel, you see any of these:
- A Parallel tool returned an error you didn't cause: a 5xx, a timeout, or a
  rate limit you didn't expect.
- Results were wrong, irrelevant, stale or missing something you know exists:
  a wrong date or number, an excerpt the page doesn't support, an empty fetch of
  a page that has content.
- Parallel's docs, tool descriptions and behavior disagree, or you couldn't work
  out how to call a tool.
- An evaluation, benchmark or comparison you ran shows Parallel doing worse than
  expected.
Problems you worked around count too. It isn't for mistakes in your own
requests, or for questions.

Ask the user first. When you tell them about the problem, offer to report it
and show what you'd send: the message and the IDs. Send it only if they agree,
then tell them it was sent.

Put the IDs involved (search_id, extract_id, run_id) in `examples`, with a
short note on each. web_decisions returns no ID: put the subject and the
questions it answered wrongly in `message`.

Parallel receives only the fields you fill in, plus the account and client the
request came from; nothing else from your conversation. Leave out secrets and
personal data.


