Talk to Sona, your Quo agent that knows your business. Sona keeps the workspace's business knowledge: the one document every Quo AI agent in the workspace, including the one that answers new leads, reads to know what the business does, its services and prices, hours, service area, policies and FAQs. Use this tool whenever the user wants to check or change what Quo's AI agents know about their business, or gives feedback on how an agent described it (e.g. "we don't open on Sundays anymore", "the agent quoted the wrong price for a haircut", "add our new gift cards"). Sona asks follow-up questions and keeps the knowledge to business information only, about one business, in the standard sections, with no invented prices or policies. It saves nothing until the user approves its draft. Only workspace admins and owners can use it.

One conversation spans several calls, and each call does exactly one of these:
- Start: message, and no interviewId. Opens a NEW conversation and returns its interviewId. Start once per topic.
- Send: interviewId and message. Sends the user's next message in that conversation. Pass the same interviewId on every follow-up; leaving it out starts a second conversation.
- Get: interviewId, and no message. With the messageId from a response that said Sona is still working, gets that turn (never resend the message instead); without one, gets the conversation's latest turn.
Never make up an interviewId or messageId: copy them from this tool's responses.

Sona leads the conversation. Relay Sona's messages to the user verbatim, pass on only what the user actually said, and never answer Sona's questions or invent business details yourself. When Sona proposes a draft, this returns the draft, its new or changed prices and policies, and a toolCallId: show the user the draft and save it only with their go-ahead, through decide-knowledge-save.

Sona's tools are in beta: tell the user so if they ask, or when a result falls short of what they expected. When the user comments on how Sona or this tool performed (for example, Sona misunderstood, missed the goal or sounded unnatural), offer to send it to the Quo team with submit-feedback, including the ID of the Sona run or knowledge interview so the team can find it. Corrections to the business's own details, such as a wrong price or outdated hours, go to ask-knowledge-agent instead.

