Query workspace-level aggregate analytics over CALLS or MESSAGES — counts, durations, segment/media counts, and rates grouped by time, user, phone number, direction, status, or outcome. Use for questions like "how many missed calls last week?", "average talk time per user", or "message volume by day". Returns summarized grouped rows only, not individual records or transcripts. Query workspace call or message analytics using the parameter schema. Returns aggregate metrics only, never individual records or transcripts.

CALL ATTRIBUTION:
- Calls have one row per associated user per call: shared-inbox calls expand per user status, including unavailable users who were not rung; calls without per-user entries have a single fallback row. Messages have one row per message.
- calls COUNT_DISTINCT grouped by user counts associated calls, including unanswered ones. A shared call can count for several users. Never sum per-user counts for a workspace total; query that total separately.
- For inbound calls handled by human teammates, group by user and filter direction EQ incoming, dialStatus EQ answered, incomingOutcome EQ answered-by-user. Use calls COUNT_DISTINCT for volume or talkDuration AVG for average answered-call talk time.
- dialStatus is per-user; status and incomingOutcome are call-level. incomingOutcome EQ answered-by-user alone can credit non-answering users. A user not answering does not mean the workspace missed the call.
- For outbound connected calls, filter direction EQ outgoing and outgoingOutcome EQ connected. Do not apply the inbound dialStatus recipe. Resolve ambiguous "handled" scope from context or ask whether it includes inbound, outbound, or both; query directions separately for both.
- Call-level durations/flags repeat across user rows. SUM/AVG/percentiles over these rows can misstate unique-call workspace metrics. talkDuration is elapsed call talk time (zero if unanswered), not per-user speaking time. ringDuration comes from the user status when available.

OUTCOMES:
incomingOutcome: answered-by-user (human answer), answered-by-agent (AI answer with talk time >= 10s), agent-abandoned (AI answer with talk time < 10s), voicemail (no answer, voicemail >= 5s), missed (no answer meeting those criteria), abandoned (caller abandoned the phone menu), forwarded (routed elsewhere); empty for outgoing calls.
outgoingOutcome: connected (answered timestamp exists), no-answer, busy, canceled, failed; empty for incoming calls. Connected does not establish a human answer or a business outcome.
actorType describes the creator/initiator, not who answered; an empty value is unknown. Use incomingOutcome to distinguish human and AI answers.

AGGREGATIONS:
Boolean SUM counts true rows; AVG is a rate from 0 to 1. Durations are seconds.
For workspace call counts and rates, use calls COUNT_DISTINCT with call-level filters. For example, voicemail rate is distinct inbound calls with incomingOutcome EQ voicemail divided by all distinct inbound calls in the same timeframe and scope, not hasVoicemail AVG over user rows.
=== entityType: "calls" ===
METRIC FIELDS + ALLOWED AGGREGATIONS:
- calls, users, phoneNumbers, conversations, fromNumbers, toNumbers → COUNT_DISTINCT
- duration, ringDuration, talkDuration, voicemailDuration (seconds) → SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, P50, P75, P90, P95, P99
- hasVoicemail, isForwarded → SUM, AVG
=== entityType: "messages" ===
METRIC FIELDS + ALLOWED AGGREGATIONS:
- messages, users, phoneNumbers, conversations, fromNumbers, toNumbers → COUNT_DISTINCT
- segments, media, recipients → SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, P50, P75, P90, P95, P99
- hasBody, hasMedia, isGroup, isAutoReply, isScheduled → SUM, AVG

TIME AND RESULTS:
- Filter createdAt with GTE start and LT end using ISO timestamps for the user's timeframe. The server requires a date filter, including for all-time requests. Use the workspace timezone, otherwise UTC. Bucket time series explicitly; createdAt defaults to TRUNCATE_MONTH when grouped without a function. Use EXTRACT_HOUR or EXTRACT_DAY_OF_WEEK for hour-of-day and day-of-week breakdowns.
- Rows align with columns; entity cells are IDs. Repeated metric fields with different aggregations use column IDs <field>_<AGGREGATION>.
- limit defaults to 50, max 200; there is no pagination. totalRows counts groups before the limit. Results sort by the groupBy fields, not metrics. Establish a workspace ranking only when results cover the requested population; otherwise explain the coverage limitation. Narrowing the timeframe or population changes the scope of the answer.
- Users with no matching calls are absent from user groups. Rankings that include zero-call teammates require a roster for the requested population; these results do not establish who was scheduled to work.
- If Quo rejects the request as invalid, this tool returns the reason as an error: correct the request and retry.

EXAMPLE — inbound calls answered by each human teammate, June 1–2 in UTC:
{
  "entityType": "calls",
  "groupBy": [{ "field": "user" }],
  "metrics": [{ "field": "calls", "aggregation": "COUNT_DISTINCT" }],
  "filters": [
    { "field": "direction", "operator": "EQ", "values": ["incoming"] },
    { "field": "dialStatus", "operator": "EQ", "values": ["answered"] },
    { "field": "incomingOutcome", "operator": "EQ", "values": ["answered-by-user"] },
    { "field": "createdAt", "operator": "GTE", "values": ["2026-06-01T00:00:00Z"] },
    { "field": "createdAt", "operator": "LT", "values": ["2026-06-03T00:00:00Z"] }
  ],
  "timezone": "UTC"
}
If a shared call rings Alice and Bob and Alice answers, only Alice gets credit in this query, even if both rows have incomingOutcome answered-by-user.

EXAMPLE — outbound message volume per day, June 1–7 in UTC:
{
  "entityType": "messages",
  "groupBy": [{ "field": "createdAt", "function": "TRUNCATE_DAY" }],
  "metrics": [{ "field": "messages", "aggregation": "COUNT_DISTINCT" }],
  "filters": [
    { "field": "direction", "operator": "EQ", "values": ["outgoing"] },
    { "field": "createdAt", "operator": "GTE", "values": ["2026-06-01T00:00:00Z"] },
    { "field": "createdAt", "operator": "LT", "values": ["2026-06-08T00:00:00Z"] }
  ],
  "timezone": "UTC"
