Send one SMS text, exactly as written, from a Quo inbox to a single recipient, right now. Use it when the user wants a specific message sent (they wrote or dictated it, or asked you to draft one) or a one-way notice such as a reminder, an address or a confirmation. It does not watch for or answer replies. To have Sona, Quo's AI agent, text someone and handle the back-and-forth until a goal is reached (confirm or reschedule an appointment, collect details, answer their questions), use start-agent-conversation instead. The `from` number must belong to the user's Quo workspace — use `list-inboxes` to discover available numbers. Recipient must be a valid phone number in E.164 format (international supported).

