Have Sona, Quo's AI agent, place a real phone call from a user's Quo number to carry out a task. Use this tool when the user asks Sona to make a call. Before using this tool, ensure the intended outcome and the details needed to achieve it are clear from the conversation. If they are ambiguous or missing, ask targeted questions; do not guess or call yet. For example, 'schedule an appointment' needs acceptable dates, times and timezone. Restate your understanding of what the agent will do and confirm the from number, destination and specific task with the user. Sona opens the call by introducing itself on behalf of the business named in the workspace's business knowledge; if no business knowledge has been added yet with ask-knowledge-agent, it introduces itself on behalf of the user, by their name. A greeting written in the task does not change this, so if the user wants Sona to introduce itself as their company, tell them to add their business knowledge with ask-knowledge-agent first. The call is real and cannot be undone. Each call uses 50 of the workspace's automation credits, or 30 prepaid credits on the agent plan (a call that ends within 15 seconds is free), so mention the cost when you confirm the call with the user; if the workspace is out of credits, the call fails without dialing. Quo may also ask the user to confirm directly. Every call needs an idempotencyKey; reuse it for every retry of the same call to avoid duplicates. This returns an agent call ID immediately while the call runs in the background. Poll get-agent-call about every 10 seconds until its status is final. Use cancel-agent-call to stop it. Sona's tools are in beta: tell the user so if they ask, or when a result falls short of what they expected. When the user comments on how Sona or this tool performed (for example, Sona misunderstood, missed the goal or sounded unnatural), offer to send it to the Quo team with submit-feedback, including the ID of the Sona run or knowledge interview so the team can find it. Corrections to the business's own details, such as a wrong price or outdated hours, go to ask-knowledge-agent instead.

