Submit this Quo workspace's draft A2P 10DLC registration to carriers. SUBMITTING IS BILLED AND IS A COMPLIANCE COMMITMENT: it charges the workspace a one-time $19.50 registration fee (paid to the Carrier Registry on the workspace's behalf; not a Quo fee), then a monthly fee of $1.50 ($3 for non-profits), and $15 for each resubmission after a rejection; the user attests the workspace will not send messages about forbidden topics (policy and fees: https://support.quo.com/getting-started/carrier-registration/carrier-registration#registration-process); and it cannot be undone through the API. It always takes TWO calls. (1) Call it with no confirmationToken: nothing is submitted or charged; it returns the registration for review, the disclosures the user must see, and a confirmationToken. Show the user every disclosure and the details, and get their explicit confirmation. (2) Only then call it again with that confirmationToken, billingAcknowledged: true and forbiddenMessageTopicsAcknowledged: true. Never set those acknowledgments without the user's explicit confirmation in this conversation. The token expires if the registration changes. If submit reports that auto-fill is still running, wait a minute and repeat step 2. Requires a workspace owner or admin and an active paid subscription.

